\subsection{Push-Pull}

As we have seen in the previous section, the push-pull property is
still necessary.  But as it turns out, our new definition of vertical
morphisms allows us to \emph{derive} push-pull for relations
that are the restriction of an identity relation along a morphism:

\begin{lemma}
  Let $f : A \to A'$ be a perturbation-preserving morphism. Then the
  relation $\restr{\ltdyn_{A'}}{f} : A \rel A'$, defined by $x \restr{\ltdyn_{A'}}{f}
  y := f x \mathrel{\ltdyn_{A'}} y$, has the push-pull property.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
  First we show how to derive push. The push homomorphism is simply
  given by $h^\to$; it remains to show the existence of the following
  square:

% https://q.uiver.app/#
\[\begin{tikzcd}[ampersand replacement=\&]
	A \& {A'} \\
	A \& {A'}
	\arrow["{\restr{\ltdyn_{A'}}{f}}", "\shortmid"{marking}, no head, from=1-1, to=1-2]
	\arrow["{i_A(m)}"', from=1-1, to=2-1]
	\arrow["{i_{A'}(h^{\to}(m))}", from=1-2, to=2-2]
	\arrow["{\restr{\ltdyn_{A'}}{f}}", "\shortmid"{marking}, no head, from=2-1, to=2-2]
\end{tikzcd}\]

By definition, it will suffice to construct a square

% https://q.uiver.app/#
\[\begin{tikzcd}[ampersand replacement=\&]
	A \& {A'} \\
	A \& {A'} \\
	{A'} \& {A'}
	\arrow["{\restr{\ltdyn_{A'}}{f}}", "\shortmid"{marking}, no head, from=1-1, to=1-2]
	\arrow["{i_A(m)}"', from=1-1, to=2-1]
	\arrow["{i_{A'}(h^{\to}(m))}", from=1-2, to=2-2]
	\arrow["f"', from=2-1, to=3-1]
	\arrow["\id", from=2-2, to=3-2]
	\arrow["{\ltdyn_{A'}}", "\shortmid"{marking}, no head, from=3-1, to=3-2]
\end{tikzcd}\]

Now since $f$ preserves perturbations, the left-hand side of the
square is equal to $i_{A'}(h^\to(m) \circ f$, so the above is the same
as

% https://q.uiver.app/#
\[\begin{tikzcd}[ampersand replacement=\&]
	A \& {A'} \\
	{A'} \& {A'} \\
	{A'} \& {A'}
	\arrow["{\restr{\ltdyn_{A'}}{f}}", "\shortmid"{marking}, no head, from=1-1, to=1-2]
	\arrow["f"', from=1-1, to=2-1]
	\arrow["\id", from=1-2, to=2-2]
	\arrow["{\ltdyn_{A'}}", "\shortmid"{marking}, no head, from=2-1, to=2-2]
	\arrow["{i_{A'}(h^{\to}(m))}"', from=2-1, to=3-1]
	\arrow["{i_{A'}(h^{\to}(m))}", from=2-2, to=3-2]
	\arrow["{\ltdyn_{A'}}", "\shortmid"{marking}, no head, from=3-1, to=3-2]
\end{tikzcd}\]

The top square exists by definition of the restriction of a relation
along a morphism, and the second square is a horizontal identity
square. Composing these vertically, we are finished.

The pull property is derived in an analogous manner.
  
\end{proof}


